f personnel engaged in research and development activities;","context":"Elements of research and development expenditures primarily include:","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":293,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"2863e1308265e0dccd0b8fcc8d947c42670a7d9071f0e71a55870e5534dae5d3","quote":"•fees for exclusive development rights of products granted to the Company;","context":"•payroll and other related costs of personnel engaged in research and development activities;","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":294,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"3635e4a56b51536746c886a3f7997d12e4e18e49dd0e4ea91287eabf715a65a5","quote":"•costs related to pre-clinical testing of the Company’s technologies and clinical trials, such as payments to CROs and CMOs, investigators, and clinical trial sites that conduct our clinical studies; and","context":"•fees for exclusive development rights of products granted to the Company;","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":295,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"2db4d51720a9c8b0c79d926ebd00106bef4b5c58d0dcc02dfb67a28fdd40e983","quote":"•costs to produce the product candidates, including raw materials and supplies, product testing, depreciation, and facility-related expenses.","context":"21","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":297,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"13bb93d65ccd2c27a211fc69d4c5d10012bcef2d178c49b81e0ca2cbb9bbe8bd","quote":"Selling, General, and Administrative Expenses","context":"•costs to produce the product candidates, including raw materials and supplies, product testing, depreciation, and facility-related expenses.","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":298,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"13cbeabbd4933afb9c50fd667285a09e7e7d190fc17c111dcd170540e36b84ee","quote":"Our selling, general, and administrative expenses consist primarily of personnel compensation and related costs, including share-based compensation for commercial and administrative personnel. Other selling, general, and administrative expenses include product distribution and promotion costs, and professional service fees for legal, intellectual property, auditing, and tax services as well as other direct and allocated expenses for rent and maintenance of facilities, insurance, and other supplies used in selling, general, and administrative activities. We expect these costs to continue to be significant to support sales of our commercial products and preparation to launch and subsequent sales of additional product candidates if and when approved.","context":"Selling, General, and Administrative Expenses","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":299,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"9c6192737404f112a3cd839534ed640b90396b1f5a21ca8af58e4e02c3a743d4","quote":"Our Ability to Commercialize Our Product Candidates","context":"Our selling, general, and administrative expenses consist primarily of personnel compensation and related costs, including share-based compensation for commercial and administrative personnel. Other selling, general, and administrative expenses include product distribution and promotion costs, and professional service fees for legal, intellectual property, auditing, and tax services as well as other direct and allocated expenses for rent and maintenance of facilities, insurance, and other supplies used in selling, general, and administrative activities. We expect these costs to continue to be significant to support sales of our commercial products and preparation to launch and subsequent sales of additional product candidates if and when approved.","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":300,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"5e8388ac5d34229b631678d6665254fcfa7664868ce852530b386cec0be1e409","quote":"We have multiple product candidates in late-stage clinical development and various others in clinical and pre-clinical development in Greater China and globally. Our ability to generate revenue from our product candidates is dependent on our receipt of regulatory approvals for and successful commercialization of such product candidates, which may not occur. Certain of our product candidates may require additional pre-clinical and/or clinical development, regulatory approvals in multiple jurisdictions, manufacturing supply, and significant marketing efforts before we generate any revenue from product sales.","context":"Our Ability to Commercialize Our Product Candidates","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":301,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-053793","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000162828026053793/zlab-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933.bin","sha256":"a35c2062944dac37c51d507089b5c79da4d68a6c25158250a8df6450c24b7933"}},{"id":"ae8f3f1f97f187d9e365356f76aa14b1829f592834af5d018db315fb702f0382","quote":"Our results of operations have been, and will continue to be, affected by our license and collaboration agreements. In accordance with these agreements, we may be required to make upfront payments and milestone payments upon the achievement of certain development, regulatory, and sales-based milestones for the relevant products as well as certain royalties at tiered percentage rates based on annual net sales of the licensed products in the licensed territories. As of June 30, 2026, we may in the future be required to pay development and regulatory milestone payments of up to an additional aggregate amount of $197.0 million for our current clinical programs and $863.0 million for other programs. Such development and regulatory milestone payments are contingent on the progress of our product candidates prior to commercialization, and we see these payments as favorable because they indicate that product candidates are advancing. As of June 30, 2026, we also in the future may be required to pay sales-based milestone payments of up to an additional aggregate amount of $3,078.0 million as well as certain royalties at tiered percentage rates on annual net sales. Such sales-based milestone and royalty payments are contingent on the performance of our commercial products, and we see these payments as favorable because they signify that a product is achieving higher sales levels.","context":"License and Collaboration Arrangements","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":303,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independentl